# Summary
Introduced: the new restart validation permits mixed primary-pending/replica-applied metadata state, but the read/authorization path was not updated to force convergence before serving snapshots from the stale primary.
Metadata commands are applied to non-primary replicas before the primary. After a crash or primary-side apply failure, the primary can retain a pending command at the next log index while other replicas have advanced. This commit changes LocalClusterMap::open to accept that mixed state as an in-flight recovery case. The problem is that opening the cluster does not immediately replay the pending command, and read-only paths such as load_bucket_snapshot read directly from the bucket metadata primary. Server authorization then derives public-read/public-write decisions from that snapshot. If the in-flight command is an access-control or public-access-block revocation, the restarted server can continue using the primary's older, more permissive bucket state until some later write path drains the pending command.

# Resolution
Fixed in `2e607a3` (`Converge in-flight metadata commands on open`).

The fix changes local-cluster open-time recovery so an accepted in-flight metadata command is converged before `LocalClusterMap::open` returns. The primary pending slot is preserved during the cluster-wide agreement check, recovery applies the command in primary-last order to match normal fanout, and the primary slot is cleaned only after required replicas have converged or the PG fails closed. This prevents read-only bucket snapshot and authorization paths from serving stale primary materialized metadata after restart.

The fix also covers the crash-step shape where the primary already has the terminal log row while a non-primary replica is still behind: reopen now keeps the pending slot as recovery intent, converges the lagging replica, and only then removes the slot. Regression coverage was added for stale snapshot prevention and terminal-primary-pending convergence. Verified with `cargo nextest run -p storage --no-fail-fast`, `./scripts/check-storage-cluster-boundaries`, and `cargo clippy --all-targets --all-features -- -D warnings`.

