## Report
Validated the suspected stale-primary metadata exposure with a targeted Rust integration PoC and an LLDB trace. Rubric checklist:
- [x] Mixed state is reachable because metadata commands apply to non-primary replicas before the primary: crates/storage/src/cluster/request_ops.rs:741-754 sorts the primary last.
- [x] Restart accepts a primary-pending/replica-applied state: crates/storage/src/cluster/local.rs:1150-1211 collects a primary pending command, and crates/storage/src/cluster/local.rs:1216-1331 returns Ok when advanced replicas match that pending command.
- [x] Open/restart does not force convergence before serving reads: the PoC reopens LocalClusterMap successfully after the injected partial apply and immediately performs a read.
- [x] Read-only bucket snapshot path reads the metadata primary directly: crates/storage/src/cluster/request_ops.rs:1229-1236 calls bucket_metadata_primary_node(...).load_bucket_snapshot, and crates/storage/src/node/bucket_ops.rs:50-57 reads the PG materialized bucket state.
- [x] Authorization-relevant state depends on that snapshot/public flag: crates/server-core/src/coordinator/authz.rs:792-794 computes effective_public_read from bucket.public_read and public_access_block.

PoC behavior: crates/storage/tests/stale_snapshot_recovery.rs creates a public-read bucket, injects StoreError::NotFound before applying a PutBucketAcl(public_read=false) command on primary node 0, leaving replicas applied and the primary with the pending slot. After dropping handles, LocalClusterMap::open succeeds. Immediately after reopen, StorageCluster::load_bucket_snapshot returns public_read=true from the stale primary. A later write path drains the pending command and public_read becomes false.

Key command output from cargo test:
`injected primary-side apply failure: Store(NotFound)`
`snapshot after reopen before drain: public_read=true`
`after write drain: public_read=false`
`test ... ok`

Debugger evidence: LLDB breakpoint at crates/storage/src/cluster/request_ops.rs:1234 after reopening showed the read-only path in StorageCluster::load_bucket_snapshot, with backtrace frame #1 at stale_snapshot_recovery.rs:53 (the post-reopen stale snapshot load). Continuing printed `snapshot after reopen before drain: public_read=true` and later `after write drain: public_read=false`.

Crash/Valgrind/Debugger attempts: this is a logic flaw, not a memory-safety crash; the targeted reproduction is non-crashing. valgrind and gdb were not installed in the container. LLDB was available and used non-interactively to trace the vulnerable read path.

